WebFPV Race Name Picker: what came from where
=============================================

This repository is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later (see LICENSE). Every source file
carries the header. This file records the parts that are somebody else's, and
how each one is held, so that the next session can see it.

The simulator's code, under sim/
--------------------------------

The race field, the post chain, the cel material, the five inch airframe, the
start block, the banner painters, the lettering and the track document
reader are WebFPVSimulator's own code (Mathew-Harvey/WebFPVSimulator,
GPL-3.0-or-later), copied byte for byte by scripts/vendor.js into sim/, laid
out from the simulator's repository root so every relative import resolves
without an edit. sim/MANIFEST.json records the simulator's commit, whether
its tree was clean when it was copied, and the SHA-256 of every file; npm run
lint fails on a file that does not match. It is regenerated, never edited. A
change the picker needs in that code is a change to the simulator.

Nothing under sim/ is the simulator's compiled flight controller or its
flight physics: the closure of what the picker imports has no WebAssembly in
it (airframes.js mentions the simulator's module in comments) and no code that
reads a gamepad. A few of its modules, race.js among them, can touch
localStorage when the simulator's own game asks them to; the picker builds
none of those objects and every storage access it makes is its own. The race
here is a plan (src/choreo.js), and nothing in this repository flies a quad
by simulation.

three.js
--------

three.js r160 and its addons (examples/jsm) are MIT licensed, Copyright (c)
2010-2023 three.js authors. They are loaded from jsDelivr by the page's
import map and are not copied into this repository. The version is the
family's and is pinned: sim/src/render/celmat.js patches one of three's shader
chunks at import and throws if the text changed.

The family's furniture
----------------------

The palette, the type stack and the lettering are the family's: the tokens
are copied from the simulator's index.html and the board's page, and the
lettering is drawn by sim/src/ui/lettering.js. No font file ships: the page
uses the system's own faces.

What is not here
----------------

No partner marks. No Betaflight name or logo: this app runs no Betaflight
code. Nothing is loaded from anywhere but the same origin and the one CDN
above, and no name or logo a person types or drops ever leaves their browser.
